*> Entity models part 2 section 3 (docs/protocol/34-entity-models-2-humanoids-zombies-skeletons-piglins.md): the layer definitions of the humanoid-base mobs.
*> Records: client/copy/CLEMM.cpy; rows are loaded by EMM-ROW (client/src/entmodel-model.cob), the base mesh by EMD-HUMANOID (client/src/entmodel-34-2.cob).
*> Entry points for the integrator (inputs):
*>   EMD-LAYER EMM-MODEL layer(X(32): ZOMBIE, ZOMBIE_BABY, HUSK, HUSK_BABY, GIANT, DROWNED, DROWNED_BABY, DROWNED_OUTER_LAYER, DROWNED_BABY_OUTER_LAYER, SKELETON, STRAY,
*>     WITHER_SKELETON, BOGGED, PARCHED, STRAY_OUTER_LAYER, BOGGED_OUTER_LAYER, PARCHED_OUTER_LAYER, PIGLIN, PIGLIN_BRUTE, ZOMBIFIED_PIGLIN, PIGLIN_BABY,
*>     ZOMBIFIED_PIGLIN_BABY, ARMOR_STAND, ARMOR_STAND_SMALL) ok(out 1 built, 0 unknown): the mesh and texture size of the layer table of 3 (scaled layers go
*>     through EMD-SCALE-ROOT, the small armor stand through EMD-BABY).
*>   EMD-STAND-ARMOR EMM-MODEL slot(1 to 4) inner outer: the armor stand's armor mesh set (3.9, 64 x 32), one slot of it.
*>   Builders (each rebuilds the model): EMD-BABY-ZOMBIE grow, EMD-DROWNED grow, EMD-SKELETON, EMD-BOGGED, EMD-PARCHED, EMD-PIGLIN, EMD-BABY-PIGLIN, EMD-ARMORSTAND.

